<title>RUSSIA: Russian VIP air carrier gets new boss.</title>
<headline>Russian VIP air carrier gets new boss.</headline>
<dateline>MOSCOW 1997-01-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>Russian President Boris Yeltsin has appointed the former head of Aeroflot International Agency, a service company for Aeroflot, as general director of Rossiya airlines, a spokeswoman for Rossiya said on Monday.</p>
<p>Vladimir Kachnov, 51, replaces Alexander Larin, as head of Rossiya, a state-owned company which operates planes transporting the president and top government officials as well as domestic and international charter passenger services.</p>
<p>-- Viktor Anoshkin, Moscow Newsroom, +7095 941 8520</p>
